Q: Use Microsoft Graph authentication to download SharePoint document by direct link (WebUrl) A: <p>I moved to using the stream from the Graph library to handle the download. This is annoying because I have to store the drive Id, item Id and version Id instead of a Url and handle them individually:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>if (currentVersion.Id == version) // Download the latest version
{
    using(Stream stream = await graphClient.Drives[drive.Id]
                .Items[item.Id]
                .Content
                .GetAsync())
    {
        await DownloadAsync(stream, localPath, item?.Size);
    }
} else // Download an old version
{
    using(Stream stream = await graphClient.Drives[drive.Id]
                .Items[item.Id]
                .Versions[version]
                .Content
                .GetAsync())
    {
        await DownloadAsync(stream, localPath, item?.Size);
    }
}
</code></pre>
